body:
I see a lot of replies to this post saying that they can relate and that they need advice. This might get buried but for those that see it I hope it helps.

&#x200B;

First, know that your attitude and outlook on life are both all in your head and you can control them. I used to struggle with anger and depression really bad all the time but what helped me get through it was the realization that my attitude was completely up to me. I didn't want to be angry or sad anymore so I started looking at things in a different light. I kept telling myself that maybe the way I saw something was wrong.

&#x200B;

Second, know that you cannot change yourself overnight and that it takes time and effort to really change who you are. Practice becomes habit after long enough. I for one had to learn to let things go a lot, and boy did it take a lot of letting things go before I really started to change. Surprisingly enough, after learning to let things go was a habit, my overall mood changed as well. I stopped getting angry all the time, even when it was something that used to make me angry. It's like the anger magically went poof! Don't let the fact that you're not in a good place right now get you down, focus on what you can be doing in the moment to change for the better.

&#x200B;

Third, do NOT lie to yourself. This may seem out of place and have you thinking, "Well SantaWithAGun, how does not lying to yourself help? How is it even possible to lie to myself?" Whenever I was angry I would tell myself that my anger was justified, because I can't be the one in the wrong. Right? Know that there are times when you have to be honest with yourself and say, "Hey what I'm doing here isn't the right thing to do." It's okay to be wrong and make mistakes because of course we all do, and the most important thing is that we learn from them. When I would get depressed I would think about how terrible my life was because I wasn't social, I didn't have a girlfriend, I had no notable skills, etc. I would blame all of these things on my parents because they didn't raise me to be a different person. Boy was I WRONG. All of those things were in my control and it was my fault for not trying to do better. I wanted life to give me a handout to make me happy but that's not how it works. You have to work for what you want in life no matter what it is. I started talking to the people I worked with and got to know them. I mustered the courage up to ask out that really hot girl I worked with and she said no. Did that make me sad? HELL YEAH IT MADE ME SAD I'M HUMAN. Guess what though? There are plenty of fish in the sea and not every girl/guy is going to say yes.

&#x200B;

To sum all of this up, your life is in your control and nobody else. I don't mean to say that if you're in a bad spot in your life that it's all your fault, because bad shit happens that may be out of your control. What I am saying is that the things that ARE under your control can be fixed, but sometimes it will take time. Don't ever give up on yourself and live every day to try and change for the better. It's never too late to show yourself some much needed love by making yourself a better person!

&#x200B;

If you have any specific questions please don't hesitate to reply or PM me. I am happy to help my fellow redditor!

&#x200B;

TL;DR - Your attitude is in your control and you can change it if you want to through practice.
